FINAL PATCH PLAN — CYCLA “TradingView-Style” ALERTS (Minimal, Professional)

──────────────────────────────────────────────
A) OVERVIEW
──────────────────────────────────────────────
Goal: Alerts button monitors all Watchlist HUD assets across their own timeframes, even when not displayed on the chart.
Keep chart untouched. Use one SSE (Server-Sent Events) stream for all symbols.

──────────────────────────────────────────────
B) RELAY PATCH  —  /signals SSE ENDPOINT
──────────────────────────────────────────────
1. Add endpoint in app.mjs:

   GET /signals?watch=ETC-USD@5m,UNI-USD@30m,LTC-USD@1D

2. Behavior:
   • Parse `watch` query param → array of {symbol, tf}.
   • For each pair, spin a TF-aware polling job using existing TwelveData + SMFT functions.
   • Reuse smft.mjs to compute arrows, printed states, and BUY/SELL markers.
   • Only emit when bar is CLOSED and marker is fully printed.
   • Emit once per bar/side (de-dupe by `symbol|tf|barTime|side`).
   • Stream lines:
       event: signal
       data: {"symbol":"LTC-USD","tf":"1D","side":"SELL","time":"2025-10-28T20:05Z","price":64.23}
   • Stagger polling intervals to respect API RPM.
   • On client disconnect, clear all timers.

3. Cadence guide:
   5m → 25s, 15m → 45s, 30m → 75s, 1H → 2min, 1D → 10min.

──────────────────────────────────────────────
C) CLIENT PATCH  —  TRADES WIDGET ALERTS
──────────────────────────────────────────────
1. On Alerts button click:
   • Build watchlist string: `symbol@tf` from HUD.
   • Open one EventSource(`/signals?watch=${list}`).
   • Store handle in global var (e.g., `window.CYCLA.alertsStream`).
   • Maintain Set for de-dupe: `symbol|tf|barTime|side`.

2. On SSE “signal” event:
   • Parse JSON {symbol, tf, side, printed, price, time}.
   • If `printed` true and not in de-dupe set:
        - Play chime.
        - Add `.tp-row--alert` pulse class on Watchlist row.
        - ECU log: `ALERT • ${symbol} • ${tf} • ${side} • ${time}`.
        - Add key to de-dupe Set.

3. On Alerts OFF:
   • Close EventSource, clear timers and de-dupe Set.

4. On Watchlist change:
   • If Alerts ON, rebuild watchlist string and reconnect SSE.

──────────────────────────────────────────────
D) UX DETAILS
──────────────────────────────────────────────
• Watchlist rows briefly pulse with glow/ring (~3s).
• Alerts button momentarily flashes when any alert fires.
• ECU messages show concise one-line summary.
• Sound only triggers after initial click to satisfy browser audio policy.

──────────────────────────────────────────────
E) DESIGN ADVANTAGES
──────────────────────────────────────────────
✓ Single persistent connection — no per-symbol polling from browser.
✓ Minimal patch: ~60 lines server + ~20 lines client.
✓ No chart edits, no Robinhood changes, no extra deps.
✓ Matches TradingView behavior: global, timeframe-aware, fully printed signals only.

──────────────────────────────────────────────
F) ACCEPTANCE CHECK
──────────────────────────────────────────────
1. Alerts OFF → silent.
2. Alerts ON with multi-timeframe Watchlist → alerts ring regardless of chart symbol.
3. De-dupe works → no double chime per bar.
4. Turning OFF stops all streams instantly.
